speechtext:
1.	Yes.
2.	Vocational Training Coordination Act-
(a)	Youth training agreement;
(b)	Apprenticeship training agreement;
(c)	Training of veterans' agreement;
(d)	Retraining of civilian workers' agreement;
(e)	Assistance to vocational schools' agreement.
Dominion-provincial farm labour programme, funds for which are provided under appropriation for Department of Labour for
1947-48.
3.	Vocational training coordination act-of the measures listed under (2) above, the province of Quebec has accepted the following:
(a)	Youth training agreement;
(c)	Training of veterans' agreement;
(e) Assistance to vocational schools' agreement.
Dominion-provincial farm labour programme.
(It is expected that Quebec will continue to participate in this programme in 1947). Note.-There is another act-the old technical education act which was extended in 1944 and calls for contribution by the province of Manitoba only. This is an extension of the original act under which all the provinces benefited but Manitoba is the only province with an unexpended credit balance remaining, and the act was extended to enable the province of Alanitoba to use up its credit.

Orders for Returns
